origin/main:docs/issues/807/runtime-refactor/work/S1-slack-channel/CHAN-A-chat-sdk-transport.md:39:The Chat SDK owns ONLY per-platform transport + native rendering. boring-agent owns ALL conversation state: message list/transcript, sessions, durable replayable event stream, follow-up queue, approvals. The bridge is a pure forwarder — every inbound event maps to a facade call (agent.start/agent.followUp/agent.resolveInput) keyed by sessionId only; every render projected from agent.stream(...). The SDK StateAdapter holds transport plumbing ONLY (dedupe keys, lock tokens, subscription flags; installation storage forbidden or encryptionKey-gated); never conversation content; AND the Chat config never enables an SDK content store (transcripts/threadHistory/messageHistory/identity/persistThreadHistory). conversationKey→sessionId lives OUTSIDE the SDK, in host state.
