origin/main:docs/issues/807/runtime-refactor/work/S1-slack-channel/CHAN-A-chat-sdk-transport.md:126:1 No SDK-owned conversation state — never the message list, sessions, durable stream, follow-up queue, or any content store (transcripts/threadHistory/messageHistory/identity/persistThreadHistory). 2 No SDK queue/debounce/burst — concurrency:'concurrent' only (guarded). 3 No @chat-adapter/state-* — our ChatTransportStateAdapter is the only StateAdapter (guarded); the owner-CAS lives on OUR ConversationSessionStore backing, not the SDK adapter. 4 No live action resolution before T1, no approval buttons — resolveInput throws ERR_NOT_IMPLEMENTED_UNTIL_T1 (createAgent.ts:171-173); ephemeral "not supported yet" (finding 11-v2), text-only render. 5 No full multi-platform build — Slack first (Discord/etc + shared-core extraction = 2nd-adapter bead per D-RATIFY-2; T2:43). 6 No new shared/core package this pass — everything in packages/channels/slack; no pi-internal reach (public facade + @hachej/boring-agent/shared types only; 08:254, WORKSPACE_CONTRACT:1-4). Scoped exception: BCH-001's DrainCoordinator lives inside @hachej/boring-agent (HarnessPiChatService) — core follow-up/run orchestration. 7 No new event protocol / render-layer rewrite (reuse AgentEvent/PiChatEvent 08:139-156,:275). 8 No durable historical-replay dependency (live-tail from startIndex P1:117). 9 No horizontal scale beyond one bridge process per conversation this pass — single-writer (§b2) is enforced; the durable pump lease for multi-replica-per-conversation is a deferred follow-up.
